{title: 634 - Come, All Christians, Be Committed}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #634 • BEACH SPRING • 8.7.9.7.8.6.8.7}
{lyricist: Eva B. Lloyd}
{composer: From The Sacred Harp}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 634}
{meta: tune BEACH SPRING}
{meta: meter 8.7.9.7.8.6.8.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Come, all Christians, [F/A]be committed
[F]To the service of the Lord;
[F/A]Make your [A7]lives [F]for him [Dm/F]more fitted,
[F]Tune your hearts with one accord.
[F]Come into [Gm]His [F]courts with gladness,
[F]Each [Dm]his sacred vows renew,
[Bb]Turn away [F]from sin and [Dm]sadness,
[F]Be transformed with life anew.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Of your time [F/C]and talents give ye,
[F]They are gifts from God above;
[F/A]To be [Dm/A]used [F]by Christians [Dm]freely
[F]To proclaim His wondrous love.
[F]Come again [Gm]to [F]serve the Savior,
[F]Tithes [Dm]and off'rings with you [Gm]bring.
[Bb]In your work, [F]with Him find [Dm]favor,
[F]And with joy His praises sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]God's command [F/C]to love each other
[F]Is required of every one;
[F/A]Showing [A7]mercy [F]to one [Dm/F]another
[F]Mirrors His redemptive plan.
[F]In compassion He has given
[F]Of His [Dm]love that is divine;
[Bb]On the cross [F]sins were forgiven;
[F]Joy and peace are fully thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Come in praise [F/C]and adoration,
[F]All who in Christ's name believe;
[F/A]Worship [Dm/A]Him [F]with consecration,
[F]Grace and love you will receive.
[F]For His grace [Gm]give [F]Him the glory,
[F]For the [Dm]Spirit and the [Gm]Word,
[Bb]And repeat [F]the gospel [Dm]story
[F]Till mankind His name has heard.
{end_of_verse}
